reviews.review:
Truly a masterpiece of the "dectective/investigator" genre.

My highlights:
- The story is actually done well and is involving;
- Diverisified puzzles that often made me feel smart when I thought outside the box, and the best part of the game for me? The [spoiler]BOMB DEFUSAL[/spoiler] puzzle.
- Extremely high quality (visuals, VA, sounds, music);
- The music;
- Interesting achievements that encourage replayability;
- Replayability: Immersion is not "broken" by players being all-knowing after an initial playthrough.

The things that I liked less:
- Too short. I understand designing the puzzles, all the visuals, doing all the research, the voice acting, etc. is incredibly time consuming, though;
- Some story beats were interesting only for the main character, but since the story is pretty short, I didn't have that same connection with some characters, so some beats were off for me;
